From acc890edd361c62e99d5e996a10d8836cc666efc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:30:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] Let REIMS_VGPU_PIPELINE_ASYNC=off build pipelines
 inside the draw

A switch, default on, so the compile-off-the-draw path can be A/B'd on
one binary. Off builds a cold graphics pipeline where the draw first
asks for it: on the drain thread, under the device and engine locks,
published before the draw goes on. No ticket is handed out and no
packet is deferred, which is how every graphics pipeline was built
before the compiler thread existed. The compile runs on the drain
breadcrumb lane, since that is the thread inside the driver.

The boot line says which arm ran (pipeline_async on=... switch=...),
REIMS_VGPU_PIPELINE_ASYNC joins env::ALL (32), and pipeline_compile
counts in_draw= beside jobs=.

Tests: lib suite 2292 passed, 0 failed (taskset 0-4,10-14, nice 19,
CARGO_TARGET_DIR ~/reims-wt/target-int2, m2v e1ffa45, llvm-dis on
PATH). New: with the switch forced off, a cold pipeline is drawn on its
first ask and counted in_draw. No guest boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
